{"step_index":20,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-01T17:04:21Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nFix a critical bug in the Ronin JLPT Vocabulary Trainer PWA where lessons never load on\nany page, under any circumstances. Root cause analysis and required fixes below — apply\nall of them, in order.\n\n## BUG 1 (root cause): loadLesson's default `level` parameter reads .value off a <div>\n\nFile: app.js, function loadLesson (around line 536):\n\n    async function loadLesson(num, level = document.getElementById('levelDropdown') ? document.getElementById('levelDropdown').value : 'n5') {\n        const res = await fetch(`data/${level}/lesson${num}.json`);\n\n`levelDropdown` is a custom `<div class=\"glass-dropdown\" id=\"levelDropdown\">` (see\nindex.html line ~184), not a native <select>. Divs have no `.value` property, so this\ndefault always evaluates to `level = undefined`, and every fetch call becomes\n`data/undefined/lessonN.json`, which 404s every time. Every call site in the app\n(`loadLesson(num)` in app.js at lines ~970, ~1487, ~1495, ~1724) omits the second\nargument, so this broken default fires on every single lesson load, on every page,\non every app start.\n\nFIX: Stop reading level from the DOM inside the function default. Instead:\n1. Introduce a single source of truth for \"currently selected level\" — e.g. a module-level\n   variable `let currentLevel = \"n5\";` (lowercase, matching the data folder names) that is\n   updated whenever the level dropdown option is clicked (in the click handler around\n   line ~1517-1524, where `levelDropSel.textContent = level` is set — update\n   `currentLevel = level.toLowerCase()` there too).\n2. Change loadLesson's signature to `async function loadLesson(num, level = currentLevel)`.\n3. Initialize `currentLevel` correctly on startup from the same logic that currently\n   computes `initialLevel` from `jlpt_lastLesson` (around line 1554-1564), and make sure\n   this runs BEFORE the startup call to loadLesson (around line 1724-1725) — currently\n   the initial `loadLesson(initLvl)` call happens using module-scope `initLvl`, so make\n   sure `currentLevel` is also set before that line executes.\n4. Rename the confusingly-named `initLvl` variable at line 1724 (it actually holds a\n   lesson NUMBER, not a level string) to `initLessonNum` to avoid future bugs like this.\n\n## BUG 2: Verify global vs per-level lesson numbering consistency\n\nFile structure: data/n5/*.json and data/n4/*.json (confirmed folders exist).\nlevelRanges in app.js (around line 1463-1469) uses GLOBAL numbering:\n    N5: [1, 25], N4: [26, 50], N3: [51, 75], N2: [76, 100], N1: [101, 125]\n\nBut loadLesson fetches `data/${level}/lesson${num}.json` — a PER-LEVEL folder path.\n\nTASK: Inspect the actual filenames inside data/n5/ and data/n4/ folders.\n- If files are named lesson1.json ... lesson25.json (relative/per-level numbering,\n  restarting at 1 for each level) — which is the more likely and more maintainable\n  scheme — then loadLesson and populateLessonOptions must convert the GLOBAL display\n  number to a RELATIVE file number before fetching. Add this conversion:\n      const range = levelRanges[level.toUpperCase()] || [1, 25];\n      const relativeNum = num - range[0] + 1;\n      const res = await fetch(`data/${level}/lesson${relativeNum}.json`);\n  Do this in loadLesson, and make sure populateLessonOptions's click handler (line ~1482-1488)\n  still passes the GLOBAL number to loadLesson (for display/storage consistency in\n  jlpt_lastLesson), letting loadLesson itself do the conversion internally.\n- If files are actually named with global numbers (lesson26.json etc. inside data/n4/),\n  no numbering fix is needed — only Bug 1's fix applies. Confirm which scheme is real\n  by listing the directory contents before deciding.\n\n## BUG 3: Clear/validate stale corrupted localStorage state\n\nBecause of Bug 1, any lesson number a user \"selected\" in the past was never actually\nsuccessfully loaded, yet loadLesson still may have left stale/inconsistent values in\nstore depending on partial execution. Additionally, real users (like the one testing\nthis app) currently have `jlpt_lastLesson: 29` stored from before these fixes existed,\nwhich will keep trying to preload a lesson that may not resolve correctly even after\nthe fix, depending on Bug 2's resolution.\n\nFIX: On app init, after determining `initialLevel` and `initLessonNum` from store,\nvalidate that `initLessonNum` actually falls within `levelRanges[initialLevel]`. If not,\nclamp it to `range[0]` (the first lesson of that level) and update the store accordingly,\nso corrupted old values self-heal instead of repeatedly failing.\n\n## BUG 4: Improve the failure path in loadLesson so failures are recoverable\n\nCurrently, on fetch failure, loadLesson (around line 571-576) only shows a toast and\nresets the *label text* to the last known-good lesson — it does NOT actually re-fetch\nand reload that lesson's data, so `vocabulary` stays empty/stale and every view\n(Home, Vocab, Review, Quiz, Games) shows 0 words until a successful load happens.\n\nFIX: In the catch block, after showing the toast, actually call\n`await loadLesson(lastWorking, level)` (guard against infinite recursion by only\nretrying once, e.g. via an internal `isRetry` parameter defaulting to false) so the\napp self-recovers to a working state instead of being left with empty vocabulary data.\n\n## TESTING CHECKLIST (verify after all fixes)\n1. Fresh load (clear localStorage) → Home page should show real word counts, not 0/20\n   with a \"not available\" toast.\n2. Switch level dropdown N5 → N4 → N3 etc. → each switch should successfully load that\n   level's first lesson with real vocabulary data (check Vocab page shows word cards,\n   not \"No words found\").\n3. Manually pick various lesson numbers from the lesson dropdown across different\n   levels → confirm each one fetches successfully (check Network tab: URLs should\n   resolve to real existing files, not data/undefined/... or 404s).\n4. Navigate between Home / Vocab / Review / Quiz / Games / Kanji / Decks tabs after a\n   successful lesson load → vocabulary should persist correctly across all views\n   without needing to reselect the lesson.\n5. Reload the page after selecting a lesson → confirm the previously selected\n   lesson/level persists and loads correctly on the next app start (jlpt_lastLesson\n   round-trips correctly through store).\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-01T22:34:21+05:30.\n\nThe user's current state is as follows:\nActive Document: e:\\JAPANESE_LANGUAGE\\JLPT Web-application\\RONIN\\index.html (LANGUAGE_HTML)\nCursor is on line: 1\nOther open documents:\n- e:\\JAPANESE_LANGUAGE\\JLPT Web-application\\RONIN\\update_html_dropdown.js (LANGUAGE_JAVASCRIPT)\n- e:\\JAPANESE_LANGUAGE\\JLPT Web-application\\RONIN\\update_css.js (LANGUAGE_JAVASCRIPT)\n- e:\\JAPANESE_LANGUAGE\\JLPT Web-application\\RONIN\\update_modals.js (LANGUAGE_JAVASCRIPT)\n- e:\\JAPANESE_LANGUAGE\\JLPT Web-application\\RONIN\\index.html (LANGUAGE_HTML)\n- e:\\JAPANESE_LANGUAGE\\JLPT Web-application\\RONIN\\update_loadlesson.js (LANGUAGE_JAVASCRIPT)\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
